# Issue #41, five releases disarmed by memory: `npm version patch` must NOT
# tag here. The tag would land on a BRANCH commit that the squash-merge to
# main discards, so v<x.y.z> would point outside the released history. The
# release tag is created on main AFTER the squash (see CLAUDE.md "Releasing").
#
# Scope, measured 2026-08-31 — this file is NOT the seatbelt:
#   * pnpm IGNORES it for `version` and tags anyway.
#   * npm honors it, but a CLI `--git-tag-version` (or an
#     `npm_config_git_tag_version=true` env var) OVERRIDES the file and tags.
# So it removes the default-path foot-gun for npm and nothing more.
# `scripts/version-guard.js` is the actual refusal, and it reads the resulting
# npm_config_git_tag_version rather than trusting this file.
git-tag-version=false
